{"category_edits":[{"category":"architecture_interaction","rationale":"Scale each feed-forward residual contribution by 0.8 across all four category models while preserving attention residuals and existing GELU sublayers. Explicit forward execution preserves the same residual formula during training and inference. The predictor writer already imports BERT4RecModel from train.py, so it automatically loads the updated architecture with unchanged checkpoint shapes.","edits":[{"find":"class BERT4RecModel(nn.Module):","replace":"class ScaledFFTransformerEncoderLayer(nn.TransformerEncoderLayer):
    def forward(self, src, src_mask=None, src_key_padding_mask=None, is_causal=False):
        x = src
        if self.norm_first:
            x = x + self._sa_block(
                self.norm1(x), src_mask, src_key_padding_mask,
                is_causal=is_causal,
            )
            x = x + 0.8 * self._ff_block(self.norm2(x))
        else:
            x = self.norm1(x + self._sa_block(
                x, src_mask, src_key_padding_mask,
                is_causal=is_causal,
            ))
            x = self.norm2(x + 0.8 * self._ff_block(x))
        return x


